I've committed the fix for #1108 as f8a34d3f. /cost now shows how much sub-agent work cost, broken down by turn, under its per-turn table. fmt, clippy (-D warnings), build and the full cargo test all pass. I haven't run it in a live REPL with a real sub_agent call.

The plan was wrong about one thing, and it made per-turn possible. The plan said sub-agent spend is only available per prompt, from the drain in audit_log_usage. That drain only runs in single-prompt mode (main.rs emit_output). In the REPL, where /cost runs, it never runs. What both modes do have is the event fired when each tool call finishes, and it carries the call's id. The same id is on the assistant message that made the call. So each sub-agent call's spend is now stored under that id, and delegated_turn_lines(messages, by_call) numbers turns the same way the existing per-turn table does, so the two line up:

```
    Sub-agent spend by turn (not in the per-turn costs above):
      Turn 2: 1 run, 12.3k in / 1.2k out, $0.042
      Total delegated: 1 run, 12.3k in / 1.2k out, $0.042
```

• No sub-agent use (most users): the function returns None and /cost is unchanged, with no block and no extra blank line. A test checks this, including that a normal tool result leaves the store empty.
• No price for the model: the turn and the total both say unpriced (not $0).
• History cleared or compacted: spend from turns that are gone gets its own "Not in the turns above" line and still counts in the total.
• Plain output: the block is plain ASCII, so it needs no separate form.

Where the code went, which differs from the plan's file list: the store and formatter are in src/prompt/sub_agent_spend.rs, where the existing sub-agent spend store already lives. The tests are in a new sibling file, src/prompt/sub_agent_spend_turn_tests.rs. The other changes are two call sites in src/prompt.rs (its line count is unchanged) and 4 lines in src/commands_info.rs. prompt_budget.rs wasn't touched.

Tests: six new tests, all fed through the real recording function and yoagent's own serialisation rather than hand-typed values. As a check, I disabled the id matching: 4 tests failed, and the 2 that only check for "nothing printed" and "ASCII only" stayed green, as they should. Then I restored it and everything passed.

Not tested: the two call-site edits in src/prompt.rs were only checked by the compiler.

Also changed:
• docs/src/features/cost-tracking.md now describes the new block and replaces the sentence saying the per-turn breakdown shows own spend only.
• tests/module_size.rs: the recorded size for commands_info.rs goes from 3542 to 3576. My change is +4 of that; the other +30 was already in the file before this change and is now recorded.
